<title>FRANCE: Roussel Uclaf says no bid decision taken.</title>
<headline>Roussel Uclaf says no bid decision taken.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>No decision has been taken on a possible bid by Germany's Hoechst on the about 45 percent of the shares it does not own in Roussel Uclaf, according to Roussel finance director Daniel Camus.</p>
<p>A weekly newspaper had suggested a 1,400 francs bid was imminent and Roussel's share surged over five percent on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Frankly, it's just another rumour. There is nothing new to my knowledge, no decision has been taken, I can therefor distance myself from this kind of information,&quot; he told Reuters.</p>
</text>
